 "source_instruction": "i would like a 3 ft long copper coaxial cable.",
 "query": "I swear I spent 20 minutes this morning chasing my neighbor\u2019s tabby cat up the oak tree at the end of my driveway, because it darted out right when I was hauling a bag of potting soil to my front porch planter. The little gremlin got all the way out to a wobbly thin branch before it froze, yowling like I was the one who\u2019d dragged it up there, and I had to balance on the lowest rung of my rickety old step ladder to coax it down with a half-eaten tuna packet I found crumpled in my jacket pocket. By the time I got it back to its owner, my jeans were smudged with tree sap, my potting soil had spilled all over the sidewalk, and I realized I\u2019d left my front door propped open the whole time, so my own dog had dragged my favorite throw blanket off the couch to chew on the corner. Right now I\u2019m over in the satellite television section. I\u2019ve heard the options that come with a coaxial cable, the short length option, and the standard build with the protective end cover in the dark colorway all clock in at no more than 40 bucks total, which lines up exactly with the setup I\u2019m currently navigating as I browse.",
